WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.701
-Welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:07.033
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.033
We got a big show tonight.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.501
Let's get to some news.
Well, guys, today New York

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:15.133
Attorney General Letitia James
announced a lawsuit against

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.801
former president Trump
and his three adult children

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.901
for allegedly committing
widespread business fraud.

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.868
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.834
You can tell Trump's worried
because he just asked

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.634
Ron DeSantis to fly him
somewhere random

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:27.667
in the middle of the night.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.701
Trump is being accused of
exaggerating

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.300
the value of his properties.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.267
The attorney general
cited a few examples.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.634
One of them being that Trump
said Mar-a-Lago is worth

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:42.400
$739 million, but it was only
appraised at $75 million.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:45.734
Trump was like,
"Technically, with all

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.000
the classified documents,
it is worth $739 million."

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.634
You took it out.

00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:00.701
Yep, $739 million, almost
10 times the actual value.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.968
Trump was going to put down
$740 million,

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.567
but he didn't want to
arouse suspicion.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.734
In response to the alleged
fraud, the State of New York

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:13.033
is now suing Trump
for $250 million.

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.567
Trump was like, "$250 million?

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.467
That's how much my fish tank
is appraised for."

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:19.701
[ Laughter ]
"Alright. Just take the tank."

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:22.300
Yes, Trump exaggerated the size
of his wealth,

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.767
his apartment,
and his properties.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.701
It's the first time he's ever
lied about how big something is.

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:30.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.334
Other than his inauguration
crowd,

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.767
his vote total,

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.601
and his night with
Stormy Daniels.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:39.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.200
"Take the fish tank.
Take the tank.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.501
I hate to see it go."

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.834
Yep, the attorney general laid
out all the details of

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.434
Trump's alleged fraud, and then
she ended her press conference

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.567
by saying this.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:54.267
-Claiming you have money
that you do not have

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:58.267
does not amount to
"The Art of the Deal."

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.100
It's the art of the steal.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.200
-Ooh.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.267
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.334
That's a burn.
-Ooh.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.400
-That's an accidentally locking
yourself in a tanning bed burn.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.601
[ Laughter ]
"Help, help."

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.300
Some more big news from here
in New York.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.734
This morning President Biden
addressed

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.601
the U.N. General assembly.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.801
In his 30-minute speech,
Biden said we need peace

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.000
between Russia and Ukraine
in Europe

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.267
and also Rachel and Tino
on "The Bachelorette."

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:28.434
We need peace.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.834
Yeah, Biden spent a good portion
of his speech on Russia.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.634
You can tell he was serious
because he was doing

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.067
that weird whisper thing.

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:37.067
[ Whispering ]
"That's why we do everything

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:40.334
[Normal voice]
to defeat Russia!"

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.434
I like that whisper thing
he does.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.200
[ Whispering ] "We've been
trying to raise money

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.000
the whole time.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.667
[ Normal voice ]
Building more bridges!"

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:53.000
Speaking of Russia, today
Vladimir Putin asked for 300,000

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.400
more troops in Ukraine,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.400
and hinted that he hasn't ruled
out a nuclear response.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.234
The only thing missing
from Putin's speech was

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.033
a cat for him
to pet the whole time.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.701
Even Kim Jong-un called.
He was like,

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.033
"Dude, you're scaring me.
What's up?"

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.067
[ Laughter ]
Let's switch gears.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:10.968
Guys, I heard that YouTube's
"dislike" and "not interested"

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:13.367
buttons don't actually stop
the platform

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.300
from showing you
similar content.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:18.968
Yeah, they're basically
the elevator door-close

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:20.000
buttons of the Internet.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.100
-He's coming, he's coming.
-Sorry.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.367
I wish I could -- Ah!
Hi, how was your weekend?

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.367
Some entertainment news.
Apparently "House of the Dragon"

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:36.467
is averaging 29 million viewers
per episode.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:37.801
-Ooh!

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.234
-But now I think
all the networks are trying

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.467
to get in on the action.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:41.901
I watched CNN this morning.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.100
Wolf Blitzer looks
a little different.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.734
Take a look.
Do you see what I'm saying?

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.601
[ Laughter ]
They're all trying to do it.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.601
-It's crazy.
-Yeah.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:51.601
Hey, guys, I read that American
Airlines just announced hackers

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.300
accessed
the personal information

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.300
of some of their customers.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.634
But you can look at it this way.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:58.734
When they use your credit card,
you still get miles.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:01.133
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.767
-And finally, speaking of
airlines, I saw that Southwest

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:06.934
surprised a full flight with
ukulele lessons

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:09.067
on a trip
from California to Hawaii.

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.634
Take a look at this.

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:13.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.567
The person in front of
the emergency exit was like,

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:16.701
"This counts, right?"

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:17.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.767
They didn't just clap
when that plane landed.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.133
They gave him
a standing ovation.

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:22.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:23.968
We have a great show, everyone.

